Add an initial conservative typed pre-VC normalizer for the experimental B3 verification backend. It preserves explicit bool/int checks, contracts and state schedules, abstracts demanded source axioms and nonidentity prelude definitions, and rejects unsupported features without producing a partial verification unit. Map equality stays opaque without extensionality. Polymorphic maps, collection definitions and lambda equations remain abstracted. A separate strict verdict runner exercises map anti-vacuity and omission controls with the packaged worker and pinned solver as a normal test-b3 stage.

The experimental B3 map slice rewrites direct closed monomorphic reads of store expressions with a source-valid conditional identity, instead of loading global quantified helper axioms. Reads through assigned variables remain conservative until a state-aware lowering is reviewed.

Exact metadata-free complete-tuple universal map-read equality uses a conservative uninterpreted observation predicate of the two map values. It adds no extensionality or pointwise observation axioms; other quantifier forms retain their original translation.
